      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We performed morphological analysis of the effect of the peptide complex from porcine kidneys on the course of experimental urolithiasis modeled in rats by treatment with 1% ethylene glycol solution (in drinking water) for 6 weeks. The peptide complex obtained by acetic acid extraction was administered in a dose of 15 mg. Administration of the peptide complex to animals with experimental kidney stone disease leads to 100% destruction of large and medium stones to the \"dust\" granularity."},
